    "title": "‘Stranger Things’ Creators’ New 8-Part Netflix Series Is Already Dominating Streaming",
    "text": "Image via Netflix Published Mar 28, 2026, 9:00 AM EDT Rohan Naahar is a Weekend News Writer for Collider. From Francois Ozon to David Fincher, he'll watch anything once. He has covered everything from Marvel to the Oscars, and Marvel at the Oscars. He also writes obsessively about the box office, charting the many hits and misses that are released weekly, and how their commercial performance shapes public perception. In his time at Collider, he has also helped drive diversity by writing stories about the multiple Indian film industries, with a goal of introducing audiences to a whole new world of cinema. Sign in to your Collider account Having recently wrapped up one of the defining shows of the last decade, the Duffer Brothers are gearing up to begin a creative partnership with Paramount. As part of their new deal, the brothers will be able to create theatrical films, which wasn't possible in their previous partnership with Netflix. However, they will always be among the streamer's most successful collaborators thanks to Stranger Things. In addition to the sci-fi series, which concluded its run at the end of 2025, the brothers have executive-produced two other shows for Netflix. May will see the release of The Boroughs, a new sci-fi show revolving around older heroes. However, the Duffers' first post-Stranger Things project debuted this week to positive reviews and an impressive audience response. Related Solve the Whodunnit in TV's Best Mystery Show Today With Collider's TV Quiz Do you know Only Murders like the back of your Arconia? We're about to find out, as you piece together the facts of this quizzical case. Collider Hailed the Duffers' New Show In Its Review Release Date March 26, 2026 Network Netflix Showrunner Haley Z. Boston Writers Haley Z. Boston Cast Creator(s) Haley Z. Boston",
